  "body": "What happens:\n\nA full parallel run of `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` fails.\nA serial run (`--test-threads=1`) passes. The failing test differs each run.\nIn one run `law_tests::gizmo_tests` fails twice (colour-scan law tests at\ncrates/ui/src/law_tests.rs:155 and :247, \"one bright and one dimmed X\").\nIn the stashed-WIP baseline run six other colour-scan tests fail\n(path_tests, preview_tests, path_lines). Serial runs of those same suites\npass.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- Full parallel run, 795 passed, 2 failed:\n  law_tests::gizmo_tests::a_moved_origin_shows_axes_and_triad_together\n  law_tests::gizmo_tests::each_triad_is_labelled_with_its_own_offset_name\n- Baseline run (WIP stashed, branch head without the uncommitted changes),\n  787 passed, 6 failed:\n  law_tests::path_tests::selecting_the_operation_brings_its_path_up\n  law_tests::path_tests::show_all_dims_instead_of_hiding\n  law_tests::path_tests::the_path_wears_the_colour_vision_palette_and_off_restores_it\n  law_tests::preview_tests::picks_are_pinned_in_the_world_not_the_window\n  law_tests::preview_tests::selecting_an_operation_outlines_its_cut_region\n  path_lines::tests::the_mark_follows_the_colour_vision_palette_and_the_dim\n\nSuspected mechanism:\n\nThe suite mutates process-global cells in parallel frames while\ncolour-scan law tests read them. Candidates:\n\n- theme::set_current / theme::current: a live OnceLock RwLock, one cell per\n  process (crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs); state.rs writes it on each\n  frame (crates/ui/src/state.rs line 4103).\n- Colour-vision state set through app commands and read by the colour-scan\n  law tests.\n\nThe structural tests already guard their mutation with\nsnapshot_guard() (crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs:1926). The colour-scan\nlaw tests do not appear to guard their reads.\n\nWhat should happen:\n\nThe parallel run must be deterministic. A fix: guard every read of the\nprocess-global theme / colour-vision cells with snapshot_guard(), or\nserialise those suites. Then pin it with repeated parallel runs (goal:\n0/30 failures across repeated full parallel runs).\n\nDone means:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` passes in repeated parallel runs\n  (>= 3 runs, 0 failures each).\n- No `#[test]` count is lost; no test is ignored or deleted to achieve this.\n\nPart of: none (follow-up found during the #1696 report-button work).\n",
